From: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5) <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: trust DT-declared exact model during match

The BPI-R4 Pro 8X declares the two AS21010PB1 PHYs with both the generic
C45 compatible and the exact fixed PHY ID:

  compatible = "ethernet-phy-id7500.9432",
               "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c45";

That fixed compatible is an explicit board-level model assertion.  Do
not still require AS21xxx match-time MMD ID reads or the generic
firmware pre-pass to discover the same model.  On r0+37890-a627bc320b
the WAN-side PHY28 eventually bound after probe-time firmware load, but
the LAN-side PHY24 still stayed on the generic C45 device and left MxL
port 13 with an empty speed mask:

  mdio-bus:18 phy_id 0x00000000 no DRIVER
  mxl862xx ... combo-lan ... support ...00006000 ... failed: -EINVAL

When DT supplies an exact AS21xxx model, skip the generic AS21xxx entry
and bind only the matching concrete AS21xxx driver entry.  Probe then
loads firmware before IPC sync, as restored by the previous patch.

This keeps non-DT and non-exact-ID users on the existing hardware-ID
discovery path while making the BPI-R4 Pro 8X fixed-ID declaration
deterministic.

Behavior source: local r0+37890-a627bc320b serial runtime evidence and
the vendor AS21xxx probe ordering.

Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5)
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -1008,6 +1008,22 @@ static int as21xxx_match_phy_device(stru
 
 	dt_phy_id = as21xxx_dt_phy_id(phydev);
 
+	if (dt_phy_id) {
+		/*
+		 * The fixed ethernet-phy-id compatible is already an exact
+		 * model assertion.  Avoid the generic firmware pre-pass and
+		 * unreliable match-time ID reads; probe will load firmware
+		 * for firmware-described DT nodes.
+		 */
+		if (phydrv->phy_id == PHY_ID_AS21XXX)
+			return 0;
+
+		if (phydrv->phy_id == dt_phy_id) {
+			phydev->phy_id = dt_phy_id;
+			return 1;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* Skip PHY that are not AS21xxx */
 	if (!phy_id_compare_vendor(phydev->c45_ids.device_ids[MDIO_MMD_PCS],
 				   PHY_VENDOR_AEONSEMI) && !dt_phy_id)
